From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:42:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 44/55] window-actor: stop counting surfaces after they leave
 the window

A window actor follows whether each of its surfaces is mapped and
obscured to decide whether the window can be seen, and lets the window
be suspended once none of them can. When a surface left the window only
its obscured handler was disconnected. Unparenting the surface then
unmapped it and the still connected mapped handler took it off the
count a second time, so the window counted one surface fewer than it
showed. With every surface it still had counted as hidden, a window in
plain sight was suspended and stopped drawing, and stayed that way
until it was closed.

From GNOME/mutter!5347.
---
 src/compositor/meta-window-actor.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compositor/meta-window-actor.c b/src/compositor/meta-window-actor.c
index d79dfb694a65105e917e8ae4463bb0d19b228292..c82a0924e2a5bb14f1e7f7f53de71b369be63db8 100644
--- a/src/compositor/meta-window-actor.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-window-actor.c
@@ -493,6 +493,9 @@ disconnect_surface_actor_from (MetaSurfaceActor *surface_actor,
   g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (surface_actor,
                                         is_surface_actor_obscured_changed,
                                         window_actor);
+  g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (surface_actor,
+                                        is_surface_actor_mapped_changed,
+                                        window_actor);
   if (meta_surface_actor_is_obscured (surface_actor))
     priv->n_obscured_surfaces--;
   if (clutter_actor_is_mapped (CLUTTER_ACTOR (surface_actor)))
